-- RDX0126: a declaration that is not `infixN <op> = path` — plan 90.
--
-- The alias is the whole point: a declaration names a function that already
-- exists. With nothing after the `=` it would emit `(a, b)` — a call to no
-- function at all — so the empty target is refused, and reported against the
-- spelling, which is the thing the author named.
infixl 6 <+> =
